          "title": "You'll want to know: 洗衣机",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "洗衣机 — xǐyījī — \"washing machine\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "我家有洗衣机 wǒ jiā yǒu xǐyījī — We've got a washing machine at home."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "洗衣机 (xǐyījī) is built from 洗 'to wash', 衣 'clothes' and 机 'machine', all three inherited from Middle Chinese, sejX, 'j+j and kj+j (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription); the dictionary glosses the last as the trigger of a crossbow, and 'machine' is a later sense."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what I do."
            }
